      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While some analyses do project severe negative impacts on sectors reliant on migrant labor, such as agriculture and construction, framing it as a guaranteed recession is an extreme prediction. Economic models vary widely in how they account for sudden labor withdrawal, with some showing sharp downturns but not necessarily a full collapse. These expert projections often rely on specific assumptions about how employers would react to labor scarcity. For a more precise view, you would need to consult recent, peer-reviewed economic impact studies specific to the proposed policy.",
