      "role": "user",
      "content": "But if the data shows these sectors are already on the brink, isn't it almost irresponsible to call it \"speculative\"? Like, if you're looking at the actual math of how much these industries contribute, the consensus among fiscal conservatives is that the cost of the current system is what's actually killing the economy. Isn't the real \"fact\" that the current status quo is unsustainable and Miller's plan is just a necessary, if painful, correction to prevent something worse?",
