      "content": "Fiscal conservative arguments often focus on the fiscal strain and perceived strains on public resources caused by current immigration levels. They may view Miller's plan as a necessary structural correction to stabilize these underlying financial issues. However, the debate centers on whether the *cost* of the status quo is greater than the *cost* of drastic policy change. Whether the current system is unsustainable or whether the proposed correction causes a fatal shock is the core point of disagreement among economists.",
